wine (11.15.0-1cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Import Wine 11.15 (upstream commit
    2df1ee28039cf84776eb1421ed90bd154cebb65f).
  * Refresh quilt patches against the new upstream tree.
  * debian/control: add mingw-w64 to Build-Depends so Wine is built with
    real PE builtins instead of .so-based placeholders; without it 64-bit
    applications fail to start in win64 prefixes ("wine: failed to open").
  * debian/control: add missing runtime Depends for X libraries that
    winex11 dlopens (libxxf86vm1, libxinerama1, libxcursor1, libxi6,
    libxcomposite1, libxfixes3) and the amd64 libasound2t64 package, so
    64-bit applications and X11 features work on minimal systems.
  * Add 0009-desktop-shell-window-only-when-shell-enabled.patch: keep the
    auto-spawned explorer.exe /desktop instance from claiming the shell
    window, so the ReactOS explorer can take the shell role in CDEX
    sessions instead of exiting at startup.
  * Add 0010-win32u-no-winlogo-icon-fallback.patch: stop exporting the
    IDI_WINLOGO placeholder to _NET_WM_ICON; the WM latched onto it and
    ignored the real icon that arrived later.
  * Add 0011-winex11-adopt-host-rect-on-maximize.patch: adopt the real
    window rect from the WM on maximize, fixing the WM unmaximizing the
    window again because Wine reported a stale, computed geometry instead.
    The adopted rect is accepted only when it intersects the virtual
    screen, so the WM's iconify animation is not mistaken for the real
    position and does not make win32u withdraw the window.

 -- Artem Lavrukhin <lavryha4590@gmail.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 19:53:34 +0300

